    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.0447v2</id>
    <title>Wiener's 'closure of translates' problem and Piatetski-Shapiro's uniqueness phenomenon</title>
    <updated>2011-07-08T19:36:45Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.0447v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0908.0447v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Wiener characterized the cyclic vectors (with respect to translations) in $l^p(Z)$ and $L^p(R)$, $p=1,2$, in terms of the zero set of the Fourier transform. He conjectured that a similar characterization should be true for $1&lt;p&lt;2$. Our main result contradicts this conjecture.</summary>
    <category term="math.CA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.FA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2009-08-04T13:58:09Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.CA"/>
    <arxiv:journal_ref>Annals of Mathematics 174 (2011), 519-541</arxiv:journal_ref>
    <author>
      <name>Nir Lev</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Alexander Olevskii</name>
    </author>
    <arxiv:doi>10.4007/annals.2011.174.1.15</arxiv:doi>
    <link rel="related" href="https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2011.174.1.15" title="doi"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6884v2</id>
    <title>Quasicrystals and Poisson's summation formula</title>
    <updated>2014-12-31T07:04:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6884v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1312.6884v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We characterize the measures on R which have both their support and spectrum uniformly discrete. A similar result is obtained in R^n for positive measures.</summary>
    <category term="math.CA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2013-12-24T20:19:42Z</published>
